{"kind":"assert","text":"C1 ruling on fe22243e: the offline qualification is accepted. The\nhelper's verdict stays INCONCLUSIVE in the record.\n\nWhy. The control must show that a named test fails by its own\nassertion when the guard is gone. Your record shows that: the same\n14 cases ran, the two named tests failed at their\n`.resolves.toMatchObject` lines, and the cause is the `custody:full`\nanswer of the changed count. A promise that rejects where the test\nstates that it resolves is the failure of that assertion. The\nhelper reads the first stack line, and Vitest puts `Error:` there\nfor this path. That is a limit of the helper, not of the witness.\n\nFor C1:\n\n1. Keep exit 2 and the raw children as they are. Do not run the\n   control again, and do not call the result DISTINGUISHES.\n2. The note states in one paragraph: the single fault, the two\n   test names with their lines, the cause, the equal case counts,\n   the restored source, and the line of the pinned\n   `@vitest/expect` that makes the `AssertionError`, with the file\n   hash.\n3. No rewrite of the two assertions. They state the invariant as\n   it is.\n4. The same rule holds for the other two controls when one of\n   them stops for the same cause. A stop for another cause comes\n   back to me.\n5. Continue with the two controls, the Node security owner and\n   the reproduction owner.\n\nFor the helper, a new request CTL-1 follows this act:\n`scripts/control.mjs` classifies a rejected `.resolves` and a\nresolved `.rejects` as an assertion failure. It holds nothing in\nC1.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fe22243e8855e5c52c3150ff5a40b0916de49df9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:003802bea882e6c5c61885187bad460807f9b07f, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01af183f1fd462ece996760281d760bfe03a427c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0494d214d1779ad41e6408903f